course: dictionary
lesson: 738
title: Context clues in a sports word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Basketball is a team game. Players bounce the ball and try to throw it through a high hoop with a net. A basketball is the large orange ball used in the game.
explain: Context helps you work out what a word means. «Basketball is played 5 a side, so 10 players are on the court.» Five players on each side makes two teams, so 10 players are on the court in all.
explain: «A full-size hoop is 3.05 m (10 feet) high.» The sentence is about height and shooting, so a hoop must be the high ring with a net that the ball goes through.
fact: Basketball is a team game played with a ball and a high hoop with a net.
fact: A team has five players on the court at once.
fact: A basket from inside the arc scores 2 points, from beyond the arc 3 points, and a free throw 1 point.
fact: Basketball was invented by James Naismith, a Canadian teacher working in the USA.
fact: Dribbling means bouncing the ball while you move, and it helps you keep control of it.
exercise: «Basketball is played 5 a side, so 10 players are on the court.» How many players are on the court in total? | 8 | 12 | *10 | 5
exercise: In basketball, how many points is a free throw worth? | 3 | 2 | 5 | *1
exercise: What is a basketball? | A tiny ball used in golf | A team of five players | A hoop with a net on top | *A large orange ball used in the game
test: In basketball, how many points is a shot from beyond the arc worth? | 4 | 1 | *3 | 2
test: What does hoop mean in «A full-size hoop is 3.05 m (10 feet) high»? | *A high ring with a net that the ball is thrown through | A type of shoe | A ball used in the game | A player who runs fast
exam: Basketball players bounce the ball while they move to keep control of it. What is this called? | Fouling | Shooting | *Dribbling | Passing
